  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1030 PM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nThe UA pattern continues to feature a suppressed high over E TX on \nSunday that later amplifies through late week. Locally, we'll be on \nthe western periphery of this growing ridge, with a redeveloping \naxis of monsoon moisture just to our west. Enough SW flow at times \nshould tug the broader moisture plume over our area which remains \nsupportive of daily rain chances, especially on the Caprock. \nTemperatures will be cooler owing to increased clouds and easterly \nwinds.\n\nUntil then, Sunday and Monday are a bit of a question mark as \nmore models drag a cold front into our northern counties by Sunday \nmorning before stalling it across the CWA in the afternoon, then \nshoving it south for Monday. NBM's winds reflect this story for the \ntime being, yet the cooler high temps won't be a factor until \nMonday, well behind the boundary. Sunday's PoPs were expanded west \nto the NM border as the front could ignite storms in this drier \nsegment. Farther east, a shearing axis of monsoon moisture with a \nweak shortwave trough favors higher PoPs in the afternoon. Monday's \nPoPs remain highest on the Caprock where moist upslope flow is \nmaximized.",
